					"elements": [
						{
							"id": "965f8f3",
							"elType": "widget",
							"widgetType": "heading",
							"settings": {
								"title": "Ken's note",
								"header_size": "p",
								"_css_classes": "eyebrow"
							},
							"elements": []
						},
						{
							"id": "6395b68",
							"elType": "widget",
							"widgetType": "text-editor",
							"settings": {
								"editor": "<p>Everybody asks for January and we understand why. But some of the best travelling we do here is in September, when the rivers are high, the country is completely green and you have the place largely to yourself.</p>\n<p>The rain in the green season is not the all-day British kind. It arrives in the afternoon, it is warm, and it is over in an hour. Plan the morning properly and the season barely costs you anything.</p>",
								"_css_classes": "bt-landing-insight__body"
							},
							"elements": []
						},
						{
							"id": "8bc4653",
							"elType": "widget",
							"widgetType": "text-editor",
							"settings": {
								"editor": "<p>Ken FJ Her — founder, Brother Tours. Licensed Lao National Tour Guide since 2010; founded Brother Tours in 2018.</p>",
								"_css_classes": "bt-landing-insight__attribution"
							},
							"elements": []
						}
